Scraps @PROJECT_VERSION@ - @SCRAPS_GAME@
====================================

A small 2D game made with the Scraps engine.

How to run
----------
Double-click scraps_client.exe, or from a command prompt in this folder:

    scraps_client                       play offline (default scene)
    scraps_client --scene <name>        play another scene from scenes/
    scraps_client --view top-down       start in another view (top-down, side, isometric)

Playing together (5 to 10 players): one person runs the server, everyone
else connects to it.

    scraps_server --scene <name> --port 7777
    scraps_client --connect <server's ip>:7777

The server needs UDP port 7777 open in the firewall of the PC it runs on.
Ctrl+C stops it.

Keys
----
    WASD or arrows    move
    Space             jump (side and isometric views)
    V                 next view (top-down, side, isometric)
    - / = or wheel    zoom
    Esc               quit

About this game
---------------
@SCRAPS_README_GAME_NOTES@
Command-line options
--------------------
scraps_client
    --scene <name>        scene to play offline
    --scene-dir <dir>     where .scene files are (default: scenes\ next to the program)
    --connect <ip:port>   join a scraps_server instead of playing offline
    --view <name>         start in top-down, side or isometric view
    --threads <n>         worker threads for the simulation (default: cores - 1; 0 = none)
    --headless            no window: run --frames frames and print a summary
    --frames <n>          quit after n frames
    --help                all options

scraps_server
    --scene <name>             scene to host
    --scene-dir <dir>          where .scene files are (default: scenes\ next to the program)
    --port <n>                 UDP port (default: 7777)
    --bind <ip>                interface to listen on (default: all; 127.0.0.1 = this PC only)
    --max-players <n>          1 to 16 (default: 10)
    --snapshot-interval <n>    ticks between snapshots (default: 1)
    --ticks <n>                stop after n ticks (default: run until Ctrl+C)
    --threads <n>              worker threads for the simulation
    --help                     all options

Scenes are plain text files in scenes\. Edit one while the game runs and it
reloads.
